# Storage Abstraction

## Core Requirements
- No direct localStorage/DB calls
- Create storage providers/services
- Isolate storage format changes

## Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// Storage Service Pattern
interface StorageService {
  get<T>(key: string): Promise<T | null>;
  set<T>(key: string, value: T): Promise<void>;
  remove(key: string): Promise<void>;
}
```

## Storage Locations
- Supabase Storage: [src/integrations/supabase](mdc:src/integrations/supabase)
- Local Storage: [src/lib](mdc:src/lib)
- Session Storage: [src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx](mdc:src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx)

## Best Practices
1. Use TypeScript for type safety
2. Implement proper error handling
3. Handle storage failures gracefully
4. Use proper data serialization
5. Implement storage cleanup

## Security Guidelines
- Never store sensitive data in localStorage
- Encrypt sensitive data before storage
- Implement proper access control
- Handle storage quotas properly
- Validate stored data on retrieval

